It is; you need Javascript enabled for it to work (I'm not even sure if
the beta works at all in Javascript-disabled browsers; Gmail doesn't and
it has the same "look and feel"). Unfortunately, it opens a new window
which is a little annoying.

Alternatively, if you're using Mozilla you can add the following to
userContent.css in the chrome directory of your profile (restart the
browser once you're done for the changes to take effect):

 /* Fixed font in Google Groups Beta */
 div.mbody {
   font-family: monospace !important;
   font-size: 14px !important;
 }

This displays all message bodies in the browser's default monospace font
(including hypertext references). The font size might be a little big,
and now that I think about it it would probably be better to specify it
in points instead of pixels.

(This was a quick rewrite of something similar for Gmail. It will break
other pages that use <div/> elements with class="mbody" and there's
probably a way of avoiding this. This trick should work in Firefox, too.)

